 ('lem:ppav-family-constant-rank-Lang-candidate','independent re-proof','PASS after the necessary reduced-base correction. For reduced locally Noetherian B, a projective-bundle open is reduced. The high iterate exponent>=b-1 has the asserted fixed geometric rank; invertible minors and vanishing of all larger minors on a reduced base give an actual image subbundle. This is a local direct summand, so pullback preserves the needed exact sequence even if Frobenius on B is not flat. F maps its Frobenius pullback into itself and is an isomorphism by fibrewise rank and Nakayama. Lang therefore gives a finite-etale local system of the exact universal rank. The whole covector theorem applies on every geometric fibre. The previous statement for an arbitrary possibly nonreduced base was too broad and is retained in the failed-scope draft.'),
 ('lem:ppav-nonordinary-strata-candidate','independent re-proof','PASS after source correction: root fully read the original EvdG Prop6.1/Lemma6.2 p601, Theorems8.1-8.2/Cor8.4 with proofs pp606-608, Lemma11.3/Thms11.4-11.5/Example11.6 pp619-620, and Example12.2 pp623-624; original620/624 actually viewed. Only the two middle final-flag maps have the required unique canonical line. The source all-four-degree1 sentence is false (ordinary gamma=p+1 on the same page); it is expressly not imported. A normal closed flag curve component is proper and generically degree1 over its ppav image, hence finite normalization, and Prop6.1 gives an actual superspecial point on it. The ppav image itself is not assumed normal. The entire existing theta/Jacobian dichotomy was reread. Cartier-zero on both genus2 canonical differentials would make their ratio a square and the canonical degree2 map purely inseparable, forcing genus0. Thus every superspecial ppav in char2 is the product E0². Level-five components, local Picard sections, and translation independence of representing principal line bundles all preserve the needed dominance and specialization.'),
 ('thm:generic-nonordinary-ppav-groups-candidate','independent re-proof','PASS: full assembly independently rederived. For f1, the smooth irreducible stratum has a normal chart through the proved mixed product at transcendental ordinary modulus. For each f0 component, its normal flag curve has the proved E0² special point. The constant-rank Lang system and full frame-component order inequality give the maximal lower bound, while the entire invariant-covector theorem gives the matching stabilizer upper bound. Thus every degree at each stated geometric generic modulus has odd GL_(9d²-1) or even Hom(F2^(f+1),F2^(9d²-4)) semidirectGL_(9d²-4). Perfect-field arithmetic covectors give arithmetic equality. Ambient restriction is explicitly conditional, with the existing regularity bound. No all-fixed-surface theorem is inferred.'),
